      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-11T13:52:41Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): judge a tool body by the band stack the simulation draws\n\nLaw (c) shank/holder reach, the (c3) mid-turn sweep and every law that\nreads verify::Cutter (solid b2, containment solid, posed rapids, rotary\nfield) now read a modelled body's band stack - the shape the fixture\nlaws sweep and the simulation draws - instead of the single cylinder\nenclosing it. The bands ride on the cutter (Cutter::body, a fixed-\ncapacity BodyBands), refused back to the cylinder when they do not fit\nthe judged record; a tool with no body reads bit-identically. Law (c)\nreports a move once per group (shank, then holder or body bands).\n\nThe drill-reach, cross-drill and probe stylus laws keep the enclosing\ncylinder and now say so by name (operation::body_judged); moving them\nis #842.\n\nFixes #835\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
