  {
    "sha": "8ca9fb6ed3ff4baa61da66413d05819e728b23b6",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDhjYTlmYjZlZDNmZjRiYWE2MWRhNjY0MTNkMDU4MTllNzI4YjIzYjY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-11T21:39:14Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-11T21:39:14Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): a leaning band's kerf stays at the tip in reach laws (c)/(c3)\n\nOn a tilted move law (c) moved each band's disc to the band's mid-axis\npoint and then excused every sample within the cutter radius of that\nmoved centre - a disc under the band, not the flutes' kerf - so a shank,\nholder or body standing in the part passed. The outer disc still stands\nat the band's centre; the excused kerf is now the cutter-radius disc\nabout the unshifted tip, in law (c), its hidden-stock backstop\n(Rest::hidden_in_annulus takes the band centre and the tip) and every\n(c3) sweep state. Upright the two coincide: vertical verdicts unchanged.\n\nverify::a_swinging_head_sweeps_the_island_wall_mid_turn: its second\nmove's end pose (shank in the island) is now convicted by (c) as\nShankHit{2, part} instead of only by (c3) as SweepHit{2, part}.\n\nPinned by tool_body_bands::{a_leaning_stepped_body_in_the_wall_is_convicted_by_law_c,\na_leaning_slim_holder_in_the_wall_is_convicted_by_law_c,\na_leaning_stepped_body_swinging_through_the_wall_is_convicted_by_law_c3,\na_leaning_slim_holder_swinging_through_the_wall_is_convicted_by_law_c3,\nupright_verdicts_are_unchanged_by_the_tip_centred_kerf}.\n\nRefs #835\nFixes #903\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
