      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-11T22:33:16Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): judge a leaning shank no wider than the cutter in reach laws (c)/(c3)\n\nLaws (c) and (c3) skipped every band with band_r <= r as \"in the\nflutes' kerf\", which holds only upright. Leaning, a plain or necked\nshank stands off the tip's column and was never judged: a long-reach\nend mill tilted 30 degrees into a wall passed with its shank in the\npart. The skip now applies only to an upright band; a leaning band of\nany positive radius is judged, the tip-centred kerf excusing the\nflutes' cut. Upright verdicts are unchanged.\n\nPinned by tool_body_bands::{a_leaning_shank_no_wider_than_the_cutter_is_convicted_by_law_c,\na_leaning_shank_no_wider_than_the_cutter_swinging_through_the_wall_is_convicted_by_law_c3,\nan_upright_shank_no_wider_than_the_cutter_reads_unchanged}.\n\nRefs #835\nFixes #903\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
